Third-party material in this repository, and what LICENSE does NOT cover
=======================================================================

LICENSE grants MIT over this project. This file names the material inside the
repository that is NOT this project's to grant, and withholds it from that
grant. It only ever takes away. Nothing here adds a permission.

WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE AND NOT A PARAGRAPH IN LICENSE

Because appending it to LICENSE would silently revoke the whole grant. GitHub's
licence detector matches LICENSE against the canonical MIT text and returns
NOASSERTION when anything follows it — this repository has already been through
that exact failure and wrote the lesson down in LICENSE-HARDWARE: "Put the
clarification beside the licence, never inside it." It matters more here than
cosmetics, because this repo is the seed of the Wish It Better network and that
network's second criterion is "a LICENSE with a real SPDX identifier", read from
the licence API. A carve-out written in good faith in the wrong file would fail
the project against the rule it wrote.


THE GUATEMALA (GT-001) CARD ARTWORK — EXCLUDED FROM THE MIT GRANT
-----------------------------------------------------------------

    src/web/templates/gt-archive-front.jpg
    src/web/templates/gt-archive-back.jpg
    src/web/templates/gt-sleek-front.jpg
    src/web/templates/gt-sleek-back.jpg

    and the same two sleek faces re-encoded as lossless PNG, at the same
    resolution, as base64 data: URIs inside src/site/gt/index.html

This artwork was commissioned from Meta AI by the card's owner and included here
at their instruction. src/web/app.js records it at the head of the GT-001
template block, which covers all four faces: "Finished artwork, placed and not
rebuilt... a card someone has already designed... the original was approved."

It is not this project's work, so this project cannot license it. Every verb the
MIT grant offers over the software — use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
distribute, sublicense, sell — is NOT offered over these files. They are present
so the owner can reprint their card and so the page the chip opens keeps working.
To reuse them, ask the owner. Where this project has re-exported or reframed a
face, that does not enlarge what may be reused — the commission underneath it is
still the owner's, and a derivative of something we cannot license is something
we cannot license.


THE EMBEDDED TYPEFACES — SIL OPEN FONT LICENSE 1.1, NOT MIT
------------------------------------------------------------

    Fragment Mono and Instrument Serif, embedded as two woff2 data: URIs inside
    src/site/gt/index.html. Full text in OFL.txt at the repo root, and served at
    https://mrdirno.github.io/vibe-cards/OFL.txt

Embedding is redistribution and subsetting to Latin is modification, so the fonts
travel under OFL 1.1 and NOT under LICENSE. Clause 5 is explicit: the Font
Software "must be distributed entirely under this license, and must not be
distributed under any other license."

This entry exists because the first draft of this file left it out and then swept
it back in by accident. That draft closed its exclusion list with "and everything
else in the tree remains MIT under LICENSE" — a sentence written to stop the
narrowing from over-reaching, which instead re-granted OFL font software under
MIT and contradicted the OFL.txt this repo ships beside it. A blanket affirmative
is how a carve-out file acquires the exact defect it was written to fix, and it
survived one draft because the file was checked for what it EXCLUDED and not for
what it QUIETLY GRANTED.


PRIOR ART CARRIED UNDER A COMPATIBLE LICENCE

src/web/vendor/qr.js states in its own header that its structure and table
